From 83f5755f62bacfaf703486a919294a14f5b034cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:31:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] swiotlb: allocate the restricted pool's slot array with 
 kvzalloc

rmem_swiotlb_device_init() allocates one struct io_tlb_slot (24 bytes on
64-bit) per 2 KiB slot of a restricted-dma-pool with kzalloc. On arm64
with 4 KiB pages kmalloc stops at 4 MiB (order 10), so a pool larger
than about 341 MiB cannot get its slot array: the page allocator warns,
the pool is not set up, and the devices that were assigned to it fall
back to direct DMA into memory the host cannot reach. In a protected
Gunyah guest every virtio device then fails; with 384 and 512 MiB pools
the VMM faulted (SIGBUS) on the first virtio-console descriptor at boot.

The slot array is only used by the CPU and need not be physically
contiguous. Allocate it with kvzalloc and free it with kvfree on the
error path.

GunyahVM needs pools above this size: a guest that renders at its
window's size keeps the backing of every graphics resource mapped in
the pool, and a full-screen GNOME desktop with full-screen GL clients
on a 3392x2400 panel needs more than 341 MiB.

Bump the guest ABI to gvm64.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/gvm-3d-guest.config | 2 +-
 kernel/dma/swiotlb.c                   | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gvm-3d-guest.config b/arch/arm64/configs/gvm-3d-guest.config
index 6a4582b418e9..f5d67a18049b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gvm-3d-guest.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gvm-3d-guest.config
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 # restricted-dma-pool (swiotlb) region: CONFIG_DMA_RESTRICTED_POOL is the one option distro kernels lack.
 CONFIG_DMA_RESTRICTED_POOL=y
 CONFIG_SWIOTLB=y
-CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-gvm63"
+CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-gvm64"
 CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO=n
 CONFIG_IKCONFIG=y
 CONFIG_IKCONFIG_PROC=y
diff --git a/kernel/dma/swiotlb.c b/kernel/dma/swiotlb.c
index 08ded023328f..55956071a233 100644
--- a/kernel/dma/swiotlb.c
+++ b/kernel/dma/swiotlb.c
@@ -1842,7 +1842,7 @@ static int rmem_swiotlb_device_init(struct reserved_mem *rmem,
 			return -ENOMEM;
 		pool = &mem->defpool;
 
-		pool->slots = kzalloc_objs(*pool->slots, nslabs);
+		pool->slots = kvzalloc_objs(*pool->slots, nslabs);
 		if (!pool->slots) {
 			kfree(mem);
 			return -ENOMEM;
@@ -1850,7 +1850,7 @@ static int rmem_swiotlb_device_init(struct reserved_mem *rmem,
 
 		pool->areas = kzalloc_objs(*pool->areas, nareas);
 		if (!pool->areas) {
-			kfree(pool->slots);
+			kvfree(pool->slots);
 			kfree(mem);
 			return -ENOMEM;
 		}
-- 
